s **NOT bound** (obsolete R1-era prose);\n- the in-tree Return Pack's `claim_ceiling` contains `NEW_EVIDENCE_COMMIT_PUBLISHED` **while**\n  `w2_evidence_commit_sha` is null — the exact prohibited prepublication combination;\n- the out-of-tree readset's TOP-LEVEL subject says `0b8ecb08` but its NESTED `publication_state.pr.head_sha`\n  still says `b8e62b96` — one manifest claiming two different current subjects.\n\n## Required product implementation (smallest existing-seam change; NO new authority/authn subsystem)\n\n1. Add a canonical request-level field `required_authn_assurance` carrying exactly `AAC1|AAC2|AAC3`.\n2. On a gated canonical request, a MISSING or MALFORMED floor must FAIL CLOSED. Do NOT silently substitute\n   AAC2. A legacy/internal adapter is permitted ONLY if it is explicit, named, and cannot let a canonical\n   request with a missing floor pass silently.\n3. `_required_authn_floor(request)` must return the exact validated request floor, never an\n   implementation-local default.\n4. The resolved `HumanGateDecision.authn_assurance_class` must meet that exact request floor.\n5. The token's authn assurance must ALSO meet the request floor and must not be weaker than the resolved\n   decision. Where the canonical source defines token `approver`/`authority_class`/authn as mirrors of the\n   current decision, reject a conflicting token value rather than trusting signed caller metadata. If the\n   source does not define such mirroring, do not invent equality semantics — record a W3 preflight TT.\n6. Do not invent an HA/AAC ranking beyond what the source defines. Use the existing\n   `AUTHN_ASSURANCE_ORDER` and the existing owner-injected authority_policy seam. If current\n   authn-context validity is required but no qualified owner interface exists, emit\n   `TEMP_CLOSED_AUTHN_CONTEXT_OWNER` with the exact missing interface rather than building a second registry.\n7. Preserve request-specific floors exactly: AAC1 stays AAC1, AAC2 stays AAC2, AAC3 stays AAC3. Do NOT\n   globally force AAC3, and do NOT preserve the old default under a new name.\n\n## Required focused tests (expected values derived from the frozen domain, not the helper)\n    A1 request AAC1 + decision AAC1 -> may pass authn floor\n    A2 request AAC2 + decision AAC1 -> DENY_AUTHN\n    A3 request AAC2 + decision AAC2 -> may pass\n    A4 request AAC3 + decision AAC2 -> DENY_AUTHN\n    A5 request AAC3 + decision AAC3 -> may pass\n    A6 canonical gated request with MISSING required_authn_assurance -> fails closed, NEVER implicit AAC2\n    A7 malformed/unknown floor (AAC9) -> deny\n    A8 CRITICAL + required AAC3 + decision/token AAC2 -> DENY_AUTHN\n    A9 CRITICAL + required AAC3 + decision/token AAC3 -> may proceed to later gates\n    A10 sufficient authority must NOT compensate for weak authn -> DENY_AUTHN\n    B1 decision meets floor but token authn below floor -> deny\n    B2 token meets floor but resolved decision below floor -> deny\n    B3 both meet the exact request floor -> proceed\n    B4 absent decision resolver -> DENY_DECISION_UNRESOLVED\n    B5 absent authority policy -> TEMP_CLOSED_AUTHORITY_RESOLUTION\n    B6 valid signature + insufficient authority -> deny\n    B7 decision belongs to another request -> deny\nHold authority/lineage constant while varying only the authn floor, so the test proves that dimension.\n\n## Must preserve (regress only, do not redesign)\n- exact PI06 §15.5 direct-concatenation basis bytes + literal vector\n  `2a868198e40141f4ccfdcf5767fcb4f5950a3c241fc04b32de7d173cb79e6992`\n- canonical `resource`/`scope` set normalization before JCS + `x-swof-collection-semantics: \"set\"` on both\n- P3/P4/P5 benign-operation floor; RUIN hard veto; UNKNOWN_RUIN safe-stop; unknown-operation safe-stop\n- RFC8785 JCS + domain frame + real Ed25519\n- owner-injected decision resolver + authority policy\n- W1 denominator 113; grand denominator >= 857; maker/checker separation\n- HGK typed acceptance resolver; non-vacuous closure; `che