{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_29","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\user\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Microsoft\\\\WindowsApps\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command '$f = \"C:'\"\\\\Projects\\\\Agent_Workspace\\\\知識庫\\\\實作相關DOC\\\\Fabric vNext\\\\Semantic World OS Fabric\\\\SWOF-F_SWOF-GENIE_All-IW_Pre-Dev_Multi-Packages\\\\PI-PKG\\\\DOC\\\\PI-PKG-06_DOC\\\\SWOF-F_SWOF-GENIE_All-IW_PI-PKG-06_DOC-03_2026-09-10_r2_FULL_REPAIR.md\\\"; \"'$l = Get-Content -LiteralPath $f; ($l[620..700] -join \"`n\")'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_29","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\user\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Microsoft\\\\WindowsApps\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command '$f = \"C:'\"\\\\Projects\\\\Agent_Workspace\\\\知識庫\\\\實作相關DOC\\\\Fabric vNext\\\\Semantic World OS Fabric\\\\SWOF-F_SWOF-GENIE_All-IW_Pre-Dev_Multi-Packages\\\\PI-PKG\\\\DOC\\\\PI-PKG-06_DOC\\\\SWOF-F_SWOF-GENIE_All-IW_PI-PKG-06_DOC-03_2026-09-10_r2_FULL_REPAIR.md\\\"; \"'$l = Get-Content -LiteralPath $f; ($l[620..700] -join \"`n\")'","aggregated_output":"  grant_id: string\n  grant_type: \"T1_LOCAL_PREGRANT\"\n  grantor_identity: identity_ref\n  grantee_identity: identity_ref\n  authority_class: enum[HA1,HA2,HA3,HA5]\n  subject_pattern: bounded_pattern\n  allowed_operations: set[operation_class]\n  allowed_resources: set[resource_ref]\n  environment: environment_id\n  max_permission_class: \"P1\"\n  max_effect_risk_tier: enum[LOW,MEDIUM]\n  purpose_ref: purpose_id\n  data_class_ceiling: data_class\n  issued_at: RFC3339_UTC\n  not_before: RFC3339_UTC\n  expires_at: RFC3339_UTC\n  revocation_generation: uint64\n  authn_assurance_floor: enum[AAC1,AAC2,AAC3]\n  nonce_namespace: string\n  integrity_profile_id: \"SWOF-HG-INTEGRITY-001\"\n  issuer_id: string\n  key_id: string\n  key_generation: uint64\n  signature: base64url_no_padding\n```\n\n**Validation:** T1 only; local P1 only; exact bounded resource set/pattern; no wildcard that can cross protected path/domain; expiry mandatory; revocation generation current; grantor still authorized; current authn meets floor. Any attempt to use this grant for P3/P4/P5, T2/T3, external write, secret access, deploy/release, rights change, irreversible deletion or physical high-impact actuation first-fails `HG-DELEGATION-NOT-APPLICABLE`.\n\n## 12.4 APPROVER_AUTHN_CONTEXT contract\n\n`ApproverAuthnContext` MUST bind provider-neutral identity, assurance class, authentication time, session generation, credential generation, enrolled-factor generation and freshness deadline. External IdP may prove authentication, but it never determines HumanGate authority. T3/P4/P5 require AAC3 unless a stricter domain profile overrides.\n\n## 12.R｜Retained r1 details under r2 closure\n\n| Authority class | Identity | Rights | Limits |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| HA1_ACCOUNTABLE_OWNER | named accountable Human | approve/deny/revoke within owned scope | cannot exceed Profile or override Ruin |\n| HA2_SCOPED_DELEGATE | named Human delegate with issuer/scope/expiry | only delegated decision classes/targets/environments | never sole approver for P4; no silent subdelegation |\n| HA3_DOMAIN_COAPPROVER | named specialist Human | required coapproval/veto for mapped domains | distinct from Maker; cannot create unrelated truth |\n| HA4_RISK_VETO_HUMAN | named Human risk/safety veto | deny/veto/safe-stop | does not mint Product/Release truth |\n| HA5_RELEASE_AUTHORITY | named Human release/promotion authority | release decision after downstream evidence | DOC-03 approval is necessary but not release PASS |\n\n**Delegation law:** explicit named Human delegate only; bind issuer, decision classes, purpose, exact scope, target/environment, validity interval, maximum risk/permission, coapproval conditions, authn floor and revocation path. GPT/model/agent/provider/tool/workflow/automation/Maker/remote agent/MCP/A2A peer is never a Human delegate. External Human authority is not imported merely because a remote system says “approved”.\n\n## 12.1 APPROVER_AUTHN_ASSURANCE_SPEC\n\n```yaml\nApproverAuthnContext:\n  authn_context_id: string\n  human_principal_ref: human_identity_ref\n  authn_assurance_class: AAC1 | AAC2 | AAC3\n  authenticated_at: timestamp\n  reauthenticated_at: timestamp\n  authn_session_generation: generation_ref\n  credential_generation: generation_ref\n  phishing_resistant: boolean\n  channel_binding_ref: integrity_ref\n  issuer_or_idp_ref: identity_provider_ref\n  expires_at: timestamp\n  evidence_ref: evidence_ref\n```\n\n### APPROVER_AUTHN_ASSURANCE_MATRIX\n\n| Class | Meaning | Minimum use |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| AAC1 | verified Human session with current identity generation | P3 LOW/MEDIUM where policy permits; lower permissions when token required |\n| AAC2 | recent strong reauthentication/MFA + current credential/session generations | P3 HIGH / sensitive domain |\n| AAC3 | recent phishing-resistant Human authentication + bound channel/device/session where supported | P4, P5 protected actions, CRITICAL effects |\n\n`HumanGatePolicy` supplies `max_reauth_age` and required AAC by action/risk/permission; there is no universal guessed duration. Commit verification rejects stale `authn_session_generation`, stale `credential_generation`, expired authn context or insufficient AAC. Compromised session/credential generation invalidates all affected pending requests/tokens. Self-approval and synthetic “human approved” text fail `DENY_FALSE_AUTHORITY`.\n# 13｜HumanGate Dual State Machines\n\n## 13.1 Dual state spaces — corrected r2 contract\n\n`HumanGateRequestState` and `ApprovalTokenState` remain separate. r2 additionally makes token issuance a third observable status so a Human decision can be valid even when minting fails.\n\n```yaml\nHumanGateRequestState: [REQUIRED, APPROVED, DENIED, CANCELLED, EXPIRED]\nTokenIssuanceStatus: [NOT_REQUIRED, PENDING, ISSUED, FAILED, INVALIDATED]\nApprovalTokenState: [ACTIVE, CONSUMED, REVOKED, EXPIRED]\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_30","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\user\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Microsoft\\\\WindowsApps\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command '$f = \"C:'\"\\\\Projects\\\\Agent_Workspace\\\\知識庫\\\\實作相關DOC\\\\Fabric vNext\\\\Semantic World OS Fabric\\\\SWOF-F_SWOF-GENIE_All-IW_Pre-Dev_Multi-Packages\\\\PI-PKG\\\\DOC\\\\PI-PKG-06_DOC\\\\SWOF-F_SWOF-GENIE_All-IW_PI-PKG-06_DOC-03_2026-09-10_r2_FULL_REPAIR.md\\\"; \"'$l = Get-Content -LiteralPath $f; ($l[760..930] -join \"`n\")'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_30","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\user\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Microsoft\\\\WindowsApps\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command '$f = \"C:'\"\\\\Projects\\\\Agent_Workspace\\\\知識庫\\\\實作相關DOC\\\\Fabric vNext\\\\Semantic World OS Fabric\\\\SWOF-F_SWOF-GENIE_All-IW_Pre-Dev_Multi-Packages\\\\PI-PKG\\\\DOC\\\\PI-PKG-06_DOC\\\\SWOF-F_SWOF-GENIE_All-IW_PI-PKG-06_DOC-03_2026-09-10_r2_FULL_REPAIR.md\\\"; \"'$l = Get-Content -LiteralPath $f; ($l[760..930] -join \"`n\")'","aggregated_output":"| T1 | show grant boundary once; noninterrupting per-operation receipts | only operations already inside signed grant | grant scope/expiry always visible and revocable |\n| T2 | deliberate ApprovalView for exact effect; progressive disclosure allowed | no scope widening; consume-once token means each new effect needs a new token/decision | prefill context may reduce typing but MUST NOT preselect approval |\n| T3 | high-salience view; consequences/irreversibility/checker status above fold | batch approval forbidden | short TTL; explicit affirm action; deny/cancel equally accessible |\n\n**Progressive disclosure law:** critical fields—operation, target, scope, data/rights impact, downside, irreversibility, rollback, permission class, T2/T3 status, required checker/coapprovers, expiry—cannot be hidden behind optional expansion. Localization may change wording, never semantics. Accessibility support MUST preserve the same fields in machine-readable accessibility tree.\n\n## 14.5 ApprovalView provenance\n\nThe runtime MUST hash the exact canonical `ApprovalDecisionBasisV1` used to render the view and record `view_render_receipt` with locale, accessibility mode, presentation schema version and field-presence bitset. UI click/chat reply/provider OAuth remains an input event only; `HumanGateDecision` is produced only after canonical mapping and authority/authn validation.\n\n## 14.R｜Retained r1 details under r2 closure\n\n`HUMAN_GATE_POLICY_SPEC` materializes deterministic rule IDs rather than placeholder prose:\n\n```yaml\nHumanGatePolicy:\n  action_class: operation_class\n  effect_risk_tier: LOW | MEDIUM | HIGH | CRITICAL | RUIN | UNKNOWN_RUIN\n  subject_risk_class: risk_class_ref\n  permission_class: P0 | P1 | P2 | P3 | P4 | P5\n  requirement_rule_id: HG-RULE-*\n  required_human_authority: authority_requirement\n  required_coapprovals: [authority_requirement]\n  required_authn_assurance: AAC1 | AAC2 | AAC3\n  max_reauth_age: duration_policy\n  decision_scope: scope_contract\n  purpose_binding: purpose_ref\n  evidence_shown_to_approver: evidence_projection_contract\n  approval_requirement_schema: ApprovalRequirementSchemaRef\n  human_gate_decision_schema: HumanGateDecisionSchemaRef\n  approval_token_schema: ApprovalTokenSchemaRef\n  expiry: expiry_policy\n  trusted_clock_profile: TrustedClockProfileRef\n  revoke: revocation_policy\n  deny: denial_policy\n  appeal: appeal_policy\n  emergency_stop: safe_stop_policy\n  reapproval_trigger: reapproval_policy_ref\n  delegated_authority_limits: delegation_contract\n  prohibited_self_approval: true\n  consumer_verification: verification_contract\n  readback: readback_contract\n  ruin_veto_relation: \"Human approval never overrides RuinHardVeto\"\n```\n\n## 14.1 ApprovalView / comprehension / accessibility contract\n\nBefore an eligible Human can decide, the surface must make available: exact action/effect, target/resource/environment, purpose, scope, data class, material evidence, plausible downside, irreversibility/blast radius, rollback/stop plan, rights/security/ruin status, coapproval requirement and token expiry. A generic Allow/Deny without effect disclosure is invalid.\n\n### APPROVAL_VIEW_REQUIREMENT_MATRIX\n\n| Requirement | Mandatory presentation / interaction rule | Invalid / first-fail condition |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Proposed operation | canonical operation/action class and effect digest visible | generic action label only |\n| Target / resource / environment | exact target context visible and token-bound | hidden or ambiguous target |\n| Scope / purpose / data class | scope widening prohibited; purpose and affected data class explicit | wildcard/broader scope than request |\n| Consequence / downside | material consequence, downside and blast radius shown | material downside omitted |\n| Rights / consent / entitlement | current generation/status summarized from IF-06D | stale/invalid rights shown as valid |\n| Ruin / Exposure | IF-06C status and hard-veto/UNKNOWN_RUIN state shown | RUIN/UNKNOWN_RUIN concealed |\n| Reversibility / rollback | reversibility class, rollback/stop path and limits disclosed | rollback represented as guaranteed when it is not |\n| Permission / effect risk | PermissionClass and EffectRiskTier shown in clear language | P3+ or CRITICAL tier hidden/downgraded |\n| Uncertainty / currentness | material uncertainty and commit-time recheck disclosed | uncertainty presented as certainty |\n| Expiry / coapprovers | request/token expiry and required coapproval visible | missing expiry/coapproval |\n| Safe alternative | lower-risk/no-effect alternative exposed where available | coercive single-path presentation |\n| Deny / cancel / safe-stop | equally reachable deny/cancel; safe-stop always identifiable | dark pattern or blocked denial |\n| Accessibility / localization | semantic accessibility and clear localized language without changing canonical IDs/digest | inaccessible or translation alters bound meaning |\n| Human comprehension record | `approval_basis_hash` binds the canonical ApprovalView projection actually shown | only click/chat/OAuth event recorded |\n\nHuman-control UX is itself a security surface:\n\n- no silent truncation of a consequential effect summary; if visual summary is shortened, the full canonical effect projection remains accessible and its digest is shown/bound;\n- screen-reader/non-visual semantics, keyboard operation and accessible safe-stop path are required for the implementation profile;\n- locale/translation mismatch must be explicit; the canonical identifiers/effect digest do not change with translation;\n- timeout/silence is not approval; accidental double-submit is idempotent at `decision_id`;\n- P4/P5/CRITICAL surfaces must not hide the downside/irreversibility section behind an unchecked default;\n- **Data minimization:** approval artifacts/logs minimize data: raw secrets/PII are forbidden, evidence is referenced, resource identifiers are redacted/pseudonymized where policy permits; privileged Human view resolves details only under its own purpose/rights scope.\n# 15｜ApprovalRequirement / HumanGateDecision / ApprovalToken Schemas\n\n## 15.1 IF-06B versioned payload family\n\nAll three canonical payloads carry ABI/schema metadata:\n\n```yaml\nif06b_version: \"1.0\"\npayload_schema_version: \"1.0.0\"\nmin_reader_version: \"1.0\"\nwriter_version: \"DOC03-r2\"\ncompatibility_class: \"STRICT_MAJOR_ADDITIVE_MINOR\"\n```\n\nUnknown fields are accepted only when `compatibility_class` and reader version permit additive fields; unknown enum values, unknown required fields, major-version mismatch or ambiguous aliases are hard failures. `semantic_version` describes the **subject**, not the ABI.\n\n## 15.2 APPROVAL_REQUIREMENT_SCHEMA_SPEC / APPROVAL_REQUIREMENT_FIELD_MATRIX — field contract\n\n| Field | Type / cardinality | Req | Owner / producer | Consumer | Validation / currentness | Security / failure / invalidation |\n|---|---|---:|---|---|---|---|\n| if06b_version | semver-ish ABI / 1 | Y | DOC-03 / classifier | all IF-06B readers | supported major | mismatch → `IF06B_VERSION_UNSUPPORTED` |\n| payload_schema_version | semver / 1 | Y | DOC-03 | validator | exact schema registry | breaking drift invalidates |\n| min_reader_version | version / 1 | Y | DOC-03 | reader | reader >= floor | reject older reader |\n| writer_version | string / 1 | Y | DOC-03 | audit/reader | recognized writer | unknown writer TEMP_CLOSED |\n| compatibil