{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_55","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\user\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Microsoft\\\\WindowsApps\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command '$f = \"C:'\"\\\\Projects\\\\Agent_Workspace\\\\知識庫\\\\實作相關DOC\\\\Fabric vNext\\\\Semantic World OS Fabric\\\\SWOF-F_SWOF-GENIE_All-IW_Pre-Dev_Multi-Packages\\\\PI-PKG\\\\DOC\\\\PI-PKG-06_DOC\\\\SWOF-F_SWOF-GENIE_All-IW_PI-PKG-06_DOC-03_2026-09-10_r2_FULL_REPAIR.md\\\"; \"'$l = Get-Content -LiteralPath $f; ($l[1116..1180] -join \"`n\")'","aggregated_output":"}\n```\n\nRuntime implementations MAY generate stricter language-native types, but they may not accept a broader value set than this registry without a versioned schema change.\n# 16｜Token Admission Invariants / Time / Integrity / Exact Binding\n\n## 16.0 Deterministic token admission invariants\n\n| ID | Condition | First-fail result |\n|---|---|---|\n| TOK-INV-001 | P3/P4/P5 without valid exact Human token | `DENY_P3_TOKEN_REQUIRED` |\n| TOK-INV-002 | subject/hash/op/target/resource/purpose/scope/data/environment mismatch | `DENY_EXACT_BINDING` |\n| TOK-INV-003 | commit time outside issuance/expiry window | `DENY_TOKEN_TIME` |\n| TOK-INV-004 | token_state != ACTIVE | `DENY_TOKEN_STATE` |\n| TOK-INV-005 | nonce/idempotency already consumed/reserved incompatibly | `DENY_REPLAY` |\n| TOK-INV-006 | rights/security/provider/authn/key/ruin generation stale | `DENY_STALE_GENERATION` |\n| TOK-INV-007 | required rollback ref unresolved | `DENY_NO_ROLLBACK` |\n| TOK-INV-008 | model/tool/provider asserts Human authority | `DENY_FALSE_AUTHORITY` |\n| TOK-INV-009 | effect = RUIN or UNKNOWN_RUIN | `HARD_VETO` / `SAFE_STOP` |\n| TOK-INV-010 | canonicalization/signature/key trust fails | `DENY_TOKEN_INTEGRITY` |\n| TOK-INV-011 | consumer audience mismatch | `DENY_AUDIENCE_MISMATCH` |\n| TOK-INV-012 | UI/protocol approve event without canonical decision/token | `DENY_FALSE_AUTHORITY` |\n| TOK-INV-013 | approver authn assurance/freshness insufficient | `DENY_AUTHN` |\n| TOK-INV-014 | AutonomyTier=T3 without current independent checker evidence | `DENY_T3_CHECKER` |\n\n\n\n## 16.1A TOKEN_TIME_VALIDITY_SPEC\n\n- `issued_at`, `reauthenticated_at`, `expires_at` are RFC3339 UTC `Z`.\n- Token admission requires `issued_at <= commit_time < expires_at`; equality at expiry is invalid.\n- Clock skew tolerance is a **health tolerance for comparing sources**, never an extension of token TTL.\n- If wall-clock uncertainty or disagreement could flip a validity decision, result is `SAFE_STOP`; no “grace approval”.\n- Contextual expiry may occur earlier than absolute expiry when any bound generation, authority, audience, effect digest or provider generation changes.\n- T3 and P4/P5 policies MAY impose shorter TTL than T2/P3; they MUST NOT impose a longer TTL than parent/domain maximum.\n\n## 16.1 SWOF-HG-INTEGRITY-001 canonical serialization\n\nCanonical token integrity is frozen as a standards-composed profile:\n\n1. Payload is UTF-8 JSON.\n2. Canonical bytes are RFC 8785 JCS over `ApprovalToken` **excluding `signature`**.\n3. JCS does not Unicode-normalize strings; producers MUST preserve exact JSON string scalar sequence. Protocol identifiers are restricted to canonical ASCII where their registry allows.\n4. Domain framing bytes are `bytes(\"SWOF:PI-PKG-06:DOC-03:APPROVAL-TOKEN:V1\\\\0\") || JCS(payload_without_signature)`.\n5. Signature algorithm is Ed25519; signature is exactly 64 raw bytes encoded Base64url without `=`.\n6. `key_id` is an opaque, case-sensitive ASCII identifier; `key_generation` is unsigned integer. Verifier resolves both from the canonical key registry.\n7. SHA-256 digests are lowercase 64-hex.\n8. Time is RFC3339 UTC; trusted-clock uncertainty beyond configured skew fails closed.\n\n## 16.2 Array semantics registry\n\n| Field | Semantics | Canonicalization |\n|---|---|---|\n| scope | set | unique; bytewise UTF-8 lexical sort of canonical atoms |\n| resource when multiple | set | unique; canonical resource ID lexical sort |\n| required_coapprovals | set | unique authority refs; lexical sort |\n| reason_codes | set | unique registered codes; lexical sort |\n| changed_basis_refs | set | unique canonical refs; lexical sort |\n| evidence_summary_ref | set unless owner marks sequence | sort canonical refs |\n| ordered workflow steps inside referenced objects | sequence | preserve owner order; never sort |\n\nSchema annotations MUST state `x-swof-collection-semantics: set|sequence`. Missing annotation on an array in a signed object is a schema error.\n\n## 16.3 TOKEN_ENVELOPE_SBB_DECISION\n\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
